XWISHES:
X
XThere are five ways to get wishes.  These are:
X
X1.  A wand of wishing  (Note for poly-pilers here:  It is no longer possible 
X    to polymorph something into a wand of wishing.)
X2.  A magic lamp - djinni appears and is grateful for his release (Also no 
X    longer possible to create via a polymorph.)
X3.  A fountain (water demon appears and is sometimes grateful for his release)
X    Water demons can be summoned by either quaffing or dipping something in
X    the fountain.  The demon will usually kill you, but I usually try quaffing
X    in all fountains with low-level characters.
X4.  Occasionally, a glowing potion will have a djinni in it who is grateful 
X    for his release.
X5.  Sitting on a throne can occasionally give you a wish.  (See THRONE EFFECTS)
X
XA successful wish places an item into your inventory.  To wish effectively, 
Xyou should wish for an item that can (literally) be placed in your inventory. 
XYou could wish for a "wide sword" and get one.  Better yet, you could wish for 
Xa "+3 wide sword" and you would at least get a wide sword. whether you get the 
Xasked for enchantments depends on a random factor that is in part, I believe, 
Xbased on your luck.  You may wish for enchantments as high as +5, but this is 
Xan all or nothing proposition.  The chances of getting higher enchantments are 
Xworse than lower enchantments, so you're better off wishing for "+2 gray 
Xdragon scale mail" than let's say "blessed +4 gray dragon scale mail."  In any 
Xcase you would get at least +0 gray dragon scale mail with the odds in your 
Xfavor for getting the +2 variety. 
X
XThe general modifiers are, of course, blessed, uncursed and cursed.  A 
Xspecific modifier for small missile weapons is poisoned (as it appears in your 
Xinventory).  Also there are named weapons (artifacts), as in a "blessed +3 
Xwide sword named Stormbringer." 
X
