XIDENTIFYING AMULETS:
X
XIdentifying amulets is a process of elimination, starting with determining 
Xwhether or not the amulet is cursed.  Determining whether it's cursed is easy 
Xenough if you're a priest or have a pet on hand.  If the amulet is cursed, 
Xdon't wear it - there are too many nasty things cursed amulets can do.  If the 
Xamulet isn't cursed, it's either an amulet of esp, life saving, reflection, or 
Xversus poison.  Try it on and see what it does.  To see if it's an amulet of 
Xesp, get blinded (put on a blindfold, quaff a potion of blindness, etc.).  If 
Xyou can suddenly see all the monsters on the level, that's what it is.  Next, 
Xfind a room away from all the monsters, and zap a wand at the wall so that it 
Xbounces at you (do this with a wand that you're immune to, or something non-
Xharmful like a sleep ray).  If your medallion reflects the ray, it's an amulet 
Xof reflection.  Finally, try eating something poisonous.  If it doesn't do you 
Xany harm, it's vs. poison.  If none of these are the case, you know it's an 
Xamulet of life saving - one of the most valuable items in the game. 
